== ARCHIVE: local CI dry-run, matrix arm pyscf=2.14.0 ==

What this is. The GitHub workflow (.github/workflows/ci.yml) has never executed, because the
repository is still private and public is the author's action to take. The three predictions
about where it would go red were made earlier; this run tests two of them locally instead of
waiting on the remote: (a) API drift in nlc_coeff / get_partition between PySCF 2.12.1 and
2.14.0, and (c) the path assumptions of the out-of-tree step.

It reproduces steps 2 and 3 of the job, verbatim, in the order the job runs them:
  step 2  python -m pytest -q                  (working tree, full suite including -m slow)
  step 3  python -m pytest -q --pyargs nlcsplit -p no:cacheprovider   (cwd /tmp)
against an install built with pip install --target ~/cilibs/p214 of pyscf==2.14.0, numpy,
pytest, plus this tree --no-deps.

Result: step 2 69 passed in 576.08s with nothing skipped; step 3 68 passed and 1 skipped in
824.43s. The skip is the S22 geometry fetch, which is by design and which only appears
out of tree, because in the working tree the downloaded geometry is present. Prediction (a)
did not materialise: 2.14.0 runs the whole suite, slow tests included, without an API error.

Why ~/cilibs and not /tmp. An earlier attempt installed into /tmp/ci214lib; WSL restarted,
/tmp was cleared, and the run silently fell back to the pyscf 2.12.1 in ~/.local while the
log still said 2.14. The header line printed by the script resolves pyscf.__file__, which is
what makes this claim checkable rather than asserted.

